== Fashion E-commerce

Global fashion e-commerce reached *770 billion USD* in 2024 and is projected to surpass *one trillion by 2030* @statista2024fashion. Despite this scale, the dominant interface, the text search bar, drives a *30 percent search abandonment rate* when customers cannot locate products through keyword queries @pinterest2023visual.

The root cause is that fashion is inherently visual. Consumers evaluate garments by aesthetic attributes -- silhouette, drape, colour relationships, and print density -- which resist capture through keyword matching. A customer can recognise a desired product in a photograph yet cannot produce query terms that retrieve it.

Industry practice confirms this mismatch. Major platforms including ASOS, Zalando, and Shopee have invested in visual search precisely because their catalogues, numbering millions of SKUs, rely on inconsistent vendor-supplied metadata for text indexing. The same garment pattern appears under different labels across vendors, silently excluding relevant products from search results.

The business case for visual search in fashion is therefore not academic: it addresses a direct revenue leakage from search abandonment. This section positions the problem domain within the broader industry context.
